init_options() {
    register_option DNF 'DNF download settings' System off append_dnf_configs 'Adds missing signature-checking, parallel-download and cleanup settings in [main]. Existing values are preserved. Editing an existing dnf.conf requires the backup-and-replace policy. Does not enable automatic yes or skip unavailable repositories.'
    register_option UPDATE 'Upgrade installed packages' System on sys_update 'Runs dnf upgrade --refresh -y. Downloads and installs available updates from enabled repositories. This can be large, and package changes are not automatically reversible. Reboot afterward if the kernel or core components changed.'
    register_option REPOS 'RPM Fusion, Terra and Flathub' System off setup_repos 'Adds third-party RPM Fusion Free/Nonfree, Terra (including extras/Mesa), and system-wide Flathub. Also upgrades the core package group. These repositories may replace distribution packages and distribute proprietary software. Package signature verification is not bypassed. Required for Steam/NVIDIA or Zed unless their repositories already exist.'
    register_option AUTO_UPDATES 'Unattended security updates' System off setup_auto_updates 'Installs the DNF automatic updater and enables its timer only when the configuration specifies security-only updates with automatic application. An existing config is kept unless you select backup-and-replace. Updates may require a manual reboot; no automatic reboot is configured.'
    register_option FAIL2BAN 'Install Fail2Ban service' Security off install_fail2ban 'Installs and starts Fail2Ban. It can ban sources that repeatedly fail authentication, but protection depends on enabled jails and matching logs. Merely enabling the daemon does not guarantee SSH protection; review jail configuration yourself.'
    register_option MAC_RAND 'Randomize network MAC addresses' Network off mac_randomization 'Sets NetworkManager defaults for random Wi-Fi scan and connection MAC addresses, including Ethernet. Existing connection profiles may override these defaults. Can break DHCP reservations, MAC allowlists and captive portals. Applied on future connections; FQS does not restart NetworkManager.'
    register_option HOSTNAME_SENDING 'Do not send DHCP hostname' Network off prevent_sending_dhcp_hostname 'Sets NetworkManager defaults to omit the machine hostname in IPv4/IPv6 DHCP. Existing connection profiles may override this. Local name registration may stop working. Takes effect on future connections.'
    register_option IPV6_PRIV 'Temporary IPv6 addresses' Network off ipv6_privacy 'Prefers temporary IPv6 addresses through NetworkManager defaults. Reduces address-based tracking, but does not hide your network prefix or identity. Existing connection settings can override it. Applies on reconnection.'
    register_option SECURE_DNS 'Strict DNS-over-TLS' Network off configure_dns_action 'Writes a systemd-resolved drop-in using an authenticated TLS provider, disables fallback resolvers and routes DNS through it. Blocks DNS if encrypted transport is unavailable; local names, captive portals and VPN DNS may break. Choose strict DNSSEC validation (yes, the default) or allow-downgrade for compatibility; downgrade mode may accept unsigned answers when validation is unavailable. Requires working systemd-resolved integration; /etc/resolv.conf is checked before execution. Only resolved is restarted, never NetworkManager.'
    register_option SYSCTL 'Advanced kernel/sysctl restrictions' Security off sysctl_hardening 'Restricts kernel introspection, BPF, io_uring, core dumps and other interfaces; enables additional memory/network protections. Can break development tools, containers, debuggers and applications. Supported settings apply immediately; unsupported keys are reported. Some restrictions cannot be undone until reboot. This is not a universally safe desktop preset.'
    register_option FLATPAK_STRICT 'Restrict all system Flatpaks' Security off strict_flatpak_overrides 'Installs Flatseal and applies global system Flatpak overrides denying host/home filesystem access and all devices. Can break GPU acceleration, games and application file access. Existing overrides are kept by default. Restore selective permissions with Flatseal, or reset global overrides with sudo flatpak override --system --reset (also removes other global customizations).'
    register_option DIS_FS 'Block uncommon filesystem modules' Security off disable_obscure_fs 'Blocks cramfs, freevxfs, jffs2, hfs and hfsplus module loading. Refuses if any is mounted or listed in fstab. Does NOT block XFS, Btrfs, ext4, optical, network or virtual filesystems. Old Mac/media formats may become unreadable. Already loaded drivers are not unloaded; reboot may be needed.'
    register_option DIS_OBSOLETE_NETWORKING 'Block legacy network protocols' Security off disable_obsolete_networking 'Blocks modules including DCCP, SCTP, RDS, TIPC, amateur-radio and CAN protocols. Specialized software, telecom tools, automotive tooling and some clusters may need these. Does not unload active modules. Remove the generated modprobe rule and reboot to restore loading.'
    register_option DIS_THUNDERBOLT 'Block legacy FireWire drivers' Hardware off disable_fireware_thunderbolt 'Blocks legacy FireWire modules to reduce DMA attack surface. FireWire disks, cameras and audio interfaces will not work after module reload/reboot. Despite the historical config filename, Thunderbolt is NOT blocked: modern docks, displays and charging may depend on it.'
    register_option DIS_GEOCLUE 'Disable location service' Security off disable_geoclue_service 'Stops and masks GeoClue if installed, independently of the desktop environment. Disables automatic location for maps, weather, time-zone changes and other clients. Restore with sudo systemctl unmask geoclue.service.'
    register_option DIS_PRINTERS 'Disable printing and local discovery' Security off disable_cups_avahi 'Stops and masks CUPS and Avahi services and activation sockets when present. Printing and multicast-DNS discovery (.local names, network devices) may stop working. Restore the needed units with systemctl unmask and enable --now.'
    register_option DIS_MODEM 'Disable mobile broadband service' Hardware off disable_modem_manager 'Stops and masks ModemManager if installed. Cellular modems/SIM mobile broadband will stop working. Does not disable Wi-Fi or Ethernet. Restore with sudo systemctl unmask ModemManager.service and enable --now.'
    register_option USBGUARD 'Enforce USB allowlist' Security off setup_usbguard 'Installs USBGuard, generates a policy as root for devices currently connected, then activates enforcement only if that desired policy is present. Connect all trusted keyboards, mice, docks and storage first. Future devices may be blocked, including input devices. Have a built-in keyboard or recovery console available. Existing rules are kept unless backup-and-replace is chosen.'
    register_option KERNEL 'Harden default kernel boot arguments' Security off hardened_kernel_args 'Adds CPU mitigations, memory initialization and strict IOMMU settings to the default kernel only. Requires at least two installed kernels and backs up boot entries. Can reduce performance or cause hardware/boot issues. Emergency shell and boot logs are retained. Select an older kernel from the boot menu if needed. New kernel installs may inherit these arguments.'
    register_option NVIDIA 'Install NVIDIA akmod driver' Hardware off install_nvidia 'Installs akmod-nvidia for a detected NVIDIA display controller. Requires RPM Fusion Nonfree. Driver compilation takes time and compatible hardware/headers; older GPUs may need legacy packages instead. Refuses when Secure Boot is enabled or cannot be checked on EFI systems: configure akmods signing/MOK manually. Do not reboot until akmods has finished.'
    register_option APPLE_KBD 'Apple keyboard: standard function keys' Hardware off hid_apple_patch 'Writes hid_apple fnmode=0 so function keys behave as standard F1-F12 keys. Applies at reboot; the currently used keyboard driver is not unloaded. Existing conflicting configuration is preserved by default.'
    register_option DRACUT 'Bluetooth keyboard initramfs config' Hardware off add_dracut_flags 'Adds the Bluetooth dracut module for future initramfs builds, only if available. Does NOT rebuild existing boot images or guarantee pairing works at the LUKS prompt. Keep a wired/built-in keyboard and a recovery kernel. Rebuild a single test image manually after reviewing your pairing requirements.'
    register_option TOR 'Install Tor daemon and browser launcher' Apps off install_tor 'Installs tor and torbrowser-launcher, then enables the Tor daemon. The launcher downloads Tor Browser on first use. Does NOT route all system traffic through Tor; use Tor Browser or explicitly configure applications. Review Tor service configuration before relying on it.'
    register_option BASH 'Custom interactive Bash prompt' Apps off setup_bash_prompt 'Appends a prompt showing time, directory and Git branch. Replaces PROMPT_COMMAND/PS1, which can conflict with shell integrations. Existing .bashrc is kept by default; backup-and-replace backs it up before appending. Applies in new shells. Symlinked .bashrc is always left alone.'
    register_option STEAM 'Steam and latest Proton-GE' Apps off setup_protonge 'Installs Steam via RPM Fusion, then downloads the latest Proton-GE from GitHub. Verifies the release-provided SHA-512 checksum and validates extraction paths. A checksum from the same source detects corruption, not a compromised publisher. Keeps an existing version directory. Restart Steam and select Proton-GE per game.'
    register_option DEV_TOOLS 'Development toolchains' Apps off add_dev_tools 'Installs kernel-devel, Android tools, Python pip/development headers, Git, Node.js/npm and Go. These packages can use substantial disk space. Does not change project environments or install global pip/npm packages.'
    register_option VIRTMANAGER 'QEMU/KVM and virt-manager' Apps off install_virtmanager 'Installs virt-manager, libvirt and QEMU/KVM, enables available libvirt sockets/service and adds you to the libvirt group if present. Hardware virtualization must be available. Group changes need a new login; libvirt access grants powerful host-management capabilities.'
    register_option GIT_SSH 'Git identity and SSH key' Apps off configure_git_action 'Sets missing global Git name/email only; existing values are always retained. Creates ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 only when neither private nor public key exists. You will be prompted for a key passphrase during execution; existing keys are never overwritten. Does not upload your public key anywhere.'
    register_option HELIUM 'Helium browser' Browser off browser_action 'Installs helium-bin from the imput/helium COPR. Enabling COPR trusts this third-party publisher. Does not remove Firefox or migrate browser data.'
    register_option TRIVALENT 'Trivalent browser' Browser off browser_action 'Adds the Secureblue RPM repository and installs Trivalent. A hardened Chromium-based browser; review upstream compatibility/security guidance. Does not remove Firefox or migrate browser data.'
    register_option BRAVE 'Brave browser with managed policies' Browser off browser_action 'Adds the official Brave RPM repository and installs Brave without executing a downloaded installer script. Adds managed policies disabling Rewards, Wallet, VPN, AI, News, Talk, Sync and Tor. Existing policy file is kept by default. Firefox and its data are retained.'
    register_option CHROMIUM 'Chromium browser' Browser off browser_action 'Installs Fedora Chromium. Does not import data, change the default browser or remove Firefox.'
    register_option LIBREWOLF 'LibreWolf browser' Browser off browser_action 'Adds the LibreWolf RPM repository and installs this privacy-oriented Firefox fork. Privacy defaults may affect website compatibility. Firefox and its profile remain untouched.'
    register_option ZED 'Zed editor' Editor off editor_action 'Installs the zed RPM package. Requires the Terra repository (select the repository option or configure Terra yourself). Existing editor configuration is not changed.'
    register_option VSCODIUM 'VSCodium editor' Editor off editor_action 'Imports the VSCodium signing key, adds its third-party RPM repository and installs codium. Existing repository configuration is kept by default. Does not migrate VS Code settings.'
